C. Random031 proof readout
  random031 has a large colored reservoir but small exact deficit: Sigma=1.831959, actual_deficit=34.928978, 8(k+cGP)+1=193.
  Phase color 0 is absent, as expected from the E=0 max-runner constraint.
  Nonzero phase colors are mirror-symmetric; the phase-branch matrix is
  symmetric after b -> 14-b and branch0 <-> branch1.
  The actual CRT witnesses hit 242 survivor gates or branch-compatible
  gate intervals, but they hit zero of the two max-delta mirror gates
  isolated by HYP-3455.  They only touch those hard components through
  lower-delta branch-opposite gates.
  Therefore the HYP-3455 seven-owner gate pair is not a colored-CRT
  survivor obstruction at V=173; it is a continuous branch-gluing proof
  obligation that the colored placement layer can route around.

D. Theorem-facing synthesis
  Old coloring route: a time t is a multiplier circular 14-coloring of
  G(Z,S).  For S3 rows, t=a/(14V) also has a phase color b=a mod 14,
  and HYP-2595 says only color-compatible V-resonances contribute to
  discrepancy.
  New branch route: the same t gives u=2t mod 1 and a branch color.
  Survivor gates are not runners; they are branch-colored pullbacks of
  multiplier colorings through the two-adic doubling map.
  Candidate lemma: any branch-colored max-delta gate obstruction with
  zero compatible phase-grid hits must discharge by colored resonance
  cancellation, a low-rank component escape, an endpoint-spine/wall
  lift, or owner-current/two-adic/signed-SPEC debt.

