F. Assumption challenge
  Considered vertices: runners, phase colors, branch colors, endpoint
  residues, gates, components, wall crossings, Fourier modes, fixed
  sections, and proof obligations.  The chosen pullback vertices preserve
  the regular circular-coloring predicate and the two-adic branch witness
  predicate simultaneously.  They destroy raw runner order and raw gate
  mass, which is legal only because the lost data is replaced by exact
  phase/branch counts, mirror checks, and hard-gate hit counts.
